# Magnus — read CURRENT_STATE first

Before **any** build-day work, planning, audit, refactor, or feature implementation in this repository:

1. **Read `docs/project/CURRENT_STATE.md` first** — completely — before opening other project docs or writing code.
2. Summarize in your reply: completed build day, stable foundations, open blockers, and what the next build day may / must not assume (from that file).
3. Then read the rest of the build-day pack as required by `magnus-project-governance.mdc` (gates, plan, open questions, prior `docs/daily/day-XX.md`, ADRs).

If `CURRENT_STATE.md` conflicts with chat memory or older paths, **`CURRENT_STATE.md` wins** until the user explicitly approves updating it.

Do not start implementation until step 1–2 are done.
